# Tracer: compiler top-level atomic equality
#
# Before (did not compile):
# sketch:
#     1 = 1
# Former compiler behavior: only forall facts inside sketch had an emitter.
#
# Now: ordinary verified equality facts may appear directly at file top level.
# Numerals and the supported `+` expression lower to Mathlib complex values;
# Litex equality lowers to Litex.Same.
#
# Boundary: this slice supports nonnegative integer numerals and `+` only.
# Other atomic predicates and arithmetic operators still fail closed.
#
# Evidence:
# target/release/litex -compact -strict -runner -f lean/examples/3_AtomicEquality.lit
# cd lean && ./compiler.sh compile examples/3_AtomicEquality.lit
# cd lean && ./compiler.sh check examples

1 = 1
2 + 3 = 5
